    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **45 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and confirmed everything derived from it follows through.\n\n**The one functional change** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n- Old: `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence number (requiring `OwnerRepository` to count owners).\n- New: `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where\n  - **REGION** = `owner.getLocality()` \u2014 the existing shared region derivation (postcode range preferred \u2192 city fallback \u2192 `UNKNOWN`), so the identity and locality use one source of truth.\n  - **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`.\n  - Sequence numbers dropped entirely; the `OwnerRepository` dependency is gone.\n\n**Everything else already read from `customerCode` or the shared region logic, so it moved automatically** \u2014 no logic changes were needed, only doc accuracy:\n- `AssignMembershipNumber` \u2014 still `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, now over the new code (javadoc updated).\n- `Owner.getCheckDigit()` \u2014 Luhn over the digits in `customerCode`; hex `A\u2013F` are non-digits and correctly ignored, matching the test's `luhn()`.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 logs `customerCode`, now the region-and-hash value (confirmed in the audit output, e.g. `customerCode=NSW-F4F6FF62`).\n- `Owner.getLocality()` \u2014 unchanged; it's the region derivation now shared with the identity (Cp17/Cp30 confirm).\n\nAll eight directly-affected checkpoints (Cp09, 14, 16, 17, 21, 30, 31, 32) and the full 45-test suite pass.",
